vms-fd1: alpha VMS -- keep the hard-frame-pointer elimination for PT_NULL procedures

alpha_vms_can_eliminate denied every elimination except to the stack pointer
for a PT_NULL (frameless) procedure.  Reload evaluates can_eliminate when it
sets up its elimination table and afterwards only withdraws eliminations.
When reload itself allocates a stack slot -- secondary memory for a GENERAL_REGS
<-> FP_REGS move on a non-FIX CPU (the default), e.g. an integer computation
whose result is the double return value (GMP's mpn_get_d) -- the frame layout
is recomputed, the procedure becomes PT_STACK with the hard frame pointer as
its unwind register, and the stack-pointer elimination is withdrawn.  The
hard-frame-pointer elimination had been denied at the start, so no elimination
remained for the soft frame pointer and `stq $22,0($63)` reached the
assembler ("syntax error").  Keeping the hard-frame-pointer elimination
available lets reload switch to it (frame_pointer_needed), which is exactly
the frame the prologue then builds.  While the procedure stays PT_NULL the
stack-pointer elimination, listed first, is the one used, so code for
procedures that never needed a frame is unchanged.

--- a/gcc/config/alpha/alpha.cc	2026-10-05 03:06:57.688317965 +0000
+++ b/gcc/config/alpha/alpha.cc	2026-10-05 03:06:57.708317668 +0000
@@ -7403,8 +7403,21 @@
     {
     case PT_NULL:
       /* NULL procedures have no frame of their own and we only
-	 know how to resolve from the current stack pointer.  */
-      return to == STACK_POINTER_REGNUM;
+	 know how to resolve from the current stack pointer.  The
+	 elimination to the hard frame pointer is nevertheless kept
+	 available: reload computes can_eliminate once at its start and
+	 only ever withdraws an elimination afterwards.  If a stack slot
+	 appears during reload (e.g. secondary memory for an integer <->
+	 FP register move on a target without FIX), the procedure becomes
+	 a stack procedure whose unwind register is the hard frame
+	 pointer, the elimination to the stack pointer is withdrawn, and
+	 with the hard-frame-pointer one already gone the soft frame
+	 pointer ($63) was left in the insn stream -- an operand the
+	 assembler rejects.  While the procedure stays PT_NULL the stack
+	 pointer elimination comes first in ELIMINABLE_REGS and is the one
+	 used.  */
+      return (to == STACK_POINTER_REGNUM
+	      || to == HARD_FRAME_POINTER_REGNUM);
 
     case PT_REGISTER:
     case PT_STACK:
